## Next.js App Router Documentation Summary

Based on the official Next.js documentation in `node_modules/next/dist/docs/`, here's a comprehensive guide covering all your questions:

### 1. How to Set Up App Directory Routing (layout.tsx, page.tsx, etc.)

**Basic Structure:**
- File-system based routing where folders define route segments
- `layout.tsx` - Shared UI across multiple pages (preserve state, remain interactive)
- `page.tsx` - Unique UI for a specific route, makes route segment publicly accessible

**Root Layout (Required):**
```tsx
// app/layout.tsx
export default function RootLayout({
  children,
}: {
  children: React.ReactNode
}) {
  return (
    <html lang="en">
      <body>{children}</body>
    </html>
  )
}
```

**Nested Routes:**
- Create folders to define URL segments
- Example: `/app/blog/[slug]/page.tsx` creates route `/blog/[slug]`
- Layouts nest automatically - child layouts wrap in parent layouts

### 2. Migration from _app.tsx and _document.tsx

**Key Changes:**
- Single `app/layout.tsx` replaces both `_app.js` and `_document.js`
- Root layout must define `<html>` and `<body>` tags
- Pages in `app` are Server Components by default (unlike Pages Router where they're Client Components)

**Migration Steps:**
1. Create `app/layout.tsx` with your global styles and providers
2. Copy contents from `_app` and `_document` into root layout
3. Context providers must be moved to Client Components
4. Use `getLayout()` pattern or convert to native nested layouts

### 3. How to Handle Metadata (Replacing next/head)

**Static Metadata:**
```tsx
// app/layout.tsx
import type { Metadata } from 'next'

export const metadata: Metadata = {
  title: 'Home',
  description: 'Welcome to Next.js',
}
```

**Dynamic Metadata with generateMetadata:**
```tsx
// app/blog/[slug]/page.tsx
export async function generateMetadata({ params, searchParams }, parent) {
  const slug = (await params).slug
  const post = await fetch(`https://api.vercel.app/blog/${slug}`).then(res => res.json())
  return {
    title: post.title,
    description: post.description,
  }
}
```

**File-based Metadata:**
- `favicon.ico`, `apple-icon.jpg`, `icon.jpg` - Favicons
- `opengraph-image.jpg`, `twitter-image.jpg` - OG images
- `robots.txt` - Search engine robots
- `sitemap.xml` - Sitemap

**Dynamic OG Images:**
```tsx
import { ImageResponse } from 'next/og'

export const size = { width: 1200, height: 630 }
export const contentType = 'image/png'

export default async function Image({ params }) {
  const post = await getPost(params.slug)
  return new ImageResponse(
    <div>{post.title}</div>
  )
}
```

### 4. How to Handle API Routes in App Router

**Route Handlers (replaces API Routes):**
- Located at `app/api/**/route.ts`
- Support GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, HEAD, OPTIONS
- Cannot coexist with `page.js` at same route level

```tsx
// app/api/route.ts
export async function GET(request: Request) {
  const res = await fetch('https://data.mongodb-api.com/...', {
    headers: {
      'Content-Type': 'application/json',
      'API-Key': process.env.DATA_API_KEY,
    },
  })
  const data = await res.json()
  return Response.json({ data })
}
```

**Caching:**
- NOT cached by default
- Opt into caching with `export const dynamic = 'force-static'`

### 5. How to Handle Dynamic Routes

**Dynamic Segments:**
```tsx
// app/blog/[slug]/page.tsx
export default async function Page({
  params,
}: {
  params: Promise<{ slug: string }>
}) {
  const { slug } = await params
  const post = await getPost(slug)
  return <div>{post.title}</div>
}
```

**Catch-all Segments:**
```tsx
// app/shop/[...slug]/page.tsx - matches /shop/a, /shop/a/b, /shop/a/b/c
export default async function Page({ params }) {
  const { slug } = await params // ['a', 'b', 'c']
}
```

**Optional Catch-all:**
```tsx
// app/shop/[[...slug]]/page.tsx - also matches /shop
export default async function Page({ params }) {
  const { slug } = await params // undefined if no slug
}
```

**In Client Components:**
```tsx
'use client'
import { use } from 'react'

export default function Page({ params }: { params: Promise<{ slug: string }> }) {
  const { slug } = use(params) // Use React's use() to unwrap promise
}
```

### 6. How Data Fetching Works (Replacing getServerSideProps, getStaticProps, getStaticPaths)

**Server-side Rendering (replacing getServerSideProps):**
```tsx
// app/dashboard/page.tsx
async function getProjects() {
  const res = await fetch(`https://...`, { cache: 'no-store' })
  return res.json()
}

export default async function Dashboard() {
  const projects = await getProjects()
  return <ul>{projects.map(p => <li key={p.id}>{p.name}</li>)}</ul>
}
```

**Static Site Generation (replacing getStaticProps):**
```tsx
// app/page.tsx - default cache is 'force-cache' (like getStaticProps)
async function getProjects() {
  const res = await fetch(`https://...`) // cached by default
  return res.json()
}

export default async function Index() {
  const projects = await getProjects()
}
```

**Incremental Static Regeneration (with revalidate):**
```tsx
async function getPosts() {
  const res = await fetch(`https://.../posts`, { 
    next: { revalidate: 60 } // revalidate every 60 seconds
  })
  return res.json()
}
```

**Dynamic Paths (replacing getStaticPaths):**
```tsx
// app/posts/[id]/page.tsx
export async function generateStaticParams() {
  return [{ id: '1' }, { id: '2' }, { id: '3' }]
}

export default async function Post({ params }) {
  const { id } = await params
  // ...
}
```

**Control Dynamic Behavior:**
```tsx
export const dynamicParams = true; // Allow undefined params (default)
// Set to false to return 404 for params not in generateStaticParams
```

**Access Request Data:**
```tsx
import { cookies, headers } from 'next/headers'

export default async function Page() {
  const theme = (await cookies()).get('theme')
  const authHeader = (await headers()).get('authorization')
}
```

### 7. How to Handle Client Components vs Server Components

**Server Components (Default):**
- Fetch data close to source
- Keep secrets safe (API keys)
- Reduce JavaScript sent to browser
- Better FCP and streaming

```tsx
// app/page.tsx - Server Component by default
export default async function Page() {
  const data = await fetch('...')
  return <div>{data}</div>
}
```

**Client Components:**
- Need interactivity, state, event handlers
- Use browser APIs (localStorage, window, etc.)
- Marked with `'use client'` directive

```tsx
'use client'
import { useState } from 'react'

export default function Counter() {
  const [count, setCount] = useState(0)
  return <button onClick={() => setCount(count + 1)}>{count}</button>
}
```

**Interleaving - Pass Server Components as Props:**
```tsx
// app/layout.tsx - Server Component
import Modal from './ui/modal' // Client Component
import Cart from './ui/cart'   // Server Component

export default function Page() {
  return (
    <Modal>
      <Cart /> {/* Server Component rendered inside Client Component */}
    </Modal>
  )
}
```

**Context Providers (Must be Client Components):**
```tsx
'use client'
import { createContext } from 'react'

export const ThemeContext = createContext({})

export default function ThemeProvider({ children }) {
  return <ThemeContext.Provider value="dark">{children}</ThemeContext.Provider>
}
```

### 8. How to Handle Navigation/Links

**Link Component:**
```tsx
import Link from 'next/link'

export default function Layout() {
  return (
    <nav>
      <Link href="/blog">Blog</Link> {/* Prefetched, no manual <a> needed */}
      <a href="/contact">Contact</a>  {/* No prefetching */}
    </nav>
  )
}
```

**Client-side Navigation (Client Component):**
```tsx
'use client'
import { useRouter, usePathname, useSearchParams } from 'next/navigation'

export default function Navigation() {
  const router = useRouter()
  const pathname = usePathname()
  const searchParams = useSearchParams()

  return (
    <button onClick={() => router.push('/blog')}>
      Go to blog
    </button>
  )
}
```

**Disabling Prefetch:**
```tsx
<Link prefetch={false} href="/blog">Blog</Link> {/* Only fetch on click */}
```

**Dynamic Routes and Search Params:**
```tsx
// Server Component page
export default async function Page({ params, searchParams }) {
  const { slug } = await params
  const filters = (await searchParams).filters // URL query parameters
}

// Client Component
'use client'
import { useSearchParams } from 'next/navigation'

export default function Filter() {
  const searchParams = useSearchParams()
  const query = searchParams.get('q')
}
```

**Streaming and Loading States:**
```tsx
// app/blog/loading.tsx
export default function Loading() {
  return <div>Loading...</div>
}

// Or use <Suspense> for granular control
import { Suspense } from 'react'

export default function Blog() {
  return (
    <Suspense fallback={<div>Loading posts...</div>}>
      <BlogList />
    </Suspense>
  )
}
```

