### Directory Structure Summary

```
/vercel/sandbox/
├── pages/
│   ├── api/
│   │   └── posts/
│   │       ├── [id].js (Dynamic API route)
│   │       └── index.js (Posts API)
│   ├── blog/
│   │   ├── [id].js (Dynamic blog post page)
│   │   └── index.js (Blog list page)
│   ├── 404.js (Custom 404 page)
│   ├── _app.js (App wrapper)
│   ├── _document.js (HTML document)
│   ├── _error.js (Error boundary)
│   └── index.js (Home page)
├── components/
│   └── AppProvider.js (Context provider)
├── styles/
│   └── globals.css (Global styles)
├── next.config.ts (Next.js config)
├── tsconfig.json (TypeScript config)
├── package.json (Dependencies)
└── .gitignore

Note: No app/ directory exists (using Pages Router only)
Note: No src/ directory exists
```

### Key Technologies and Styling Approach

- **Framework**: Next.js 16.2.0-canary.41 (Pages Router pattern)
- **UI Library**: React 19.1.0
- **Styling**: Plain CSS (globals.css) - no CSS-in-JS or preprocessors
- **Type Checking**: TypeScript with strict mode enabled
- **Context API**: Custom AppProvider for theme state management
- **Data Fetching**: Mix of SSR (getServerSideProps), SSG (getStaticProps), and ISR
- **External Data**: JSONPlaceholder API for blog content
- **Font**: Google Fonts (Inter)
- **AI SDK**: Installed dependencies for @ai-sdk/react and ai, but not currently used in pages

